<title>USA: Fed seen staying out of banking system Friday.</title>
<headline>Fed seen staying out of banking system Friday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve was seen remaining on the sidelines during its usual midmorning intervention period Friday.</p>
<p>Economists said the 14-day fixed-system repurchase agreement executed Thursday was probably sufficient to meet the Fed's add need until Tuesday.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-1/8 percent, below the Fed's current official target level of 5-1/4 percent.</p>
<p>(( J. Hughes, N.A. Treasury desk, 212-859-1663))</p>
